        "topFinding": "The reliability and performance work actually moved: 14 commits (2026-08-14 to 2026-08-16) verifiably fixed 10 of the last review's findings, including the two real bug-risk items (the day_unavailability cascade and the shifts.ts remove/add batching) that were the main reason the last verdict was needs-attention. Reliability jumped 64 to 80, performance 62 to 82, kv-data-shape 66 to 90, auth-token-hygiene 80 to 92, audit-loop-integrity 60 to 95. But none of that work touched the actual gate: strategic-kill-this cratered from 35 to 15 because a full release cycle had the capacity to move either the real-use-testing or the payment-integration gate item and spent all of it on bar-raise backlog instead, while the freeze recommendation from the last run was silently ignored rather than honored or overruled. Separately, this run surfaced that the personal-skills plugin runtime copy is NUL-truncated, which explains a live bug in git-unstick's repo-path table and drags several orchestration-lens scores down with it. Health is flat at 68 (was 69) because real code fixes were offset almost exactly by newly-discovered orchestration and strategic debt.",
